What happened
  Your wallet is not approved to move that much USDC: it is allowed 0 USDC and the transaction needed 0.000001 USDC.

Why
  Moving tokens on someone else's behalf needs their permission first (an "approval" that sets how much the spender may take). Your wallet was allowed 0 USDC but tried to take 0.000001 USDC, so the token contract stopped it.

What you can do
  - The token's owner must approve first: from the owner's wallet call approve(0x317bca01Bb101C0F1E86C21576a4e14D92B02975, 0.000001 USDC or more) on the token 0xE0BE08c77f415F577A1B3A9aD7a1Df1479564ec8, wait for it to confirm, then send this transaction again.
  - Approve only the amount you need, not an unlimited amount.

